    <content>
        <subject>surveys</subject>
        <description>The DECam Local Volume Exploration Survey Data Release 2 (DELVE DR2) combines new DECam observations with archival DECam data from the Dark Energy Survey, the DECam Legacy Survey, and other DECam community programs to study dwarf satellite galaxies over a wide range of luminosities and environments. It consists of ~160,000 exposures that cover >21,000 deg^2 of the high Galactic latitude (|b| > 10 deg) sky in four broadband optical/near-infrared filters (g, r, i, z), with point-source and automatic aperture photometry for ~2.5 billion astronomical sources.</description>
        <referenceURL>https://datalab.noirlab.edu/delve/index.php</referenceURL>
        <type>Archive</type>
        <contentLevel>Research</contentLevel>
    </content>
